   "date": "2018-04-04T21:01:01Z",
   "subject": "Coefficient estimates are unstandardized?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Am I correct that the coefficient estimates in the brms output (i.e., the Estimate column) are unstandardized?<div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve found some guidelines for setting priors on standardized regression coefficients. Is there a way to adopt this to brms (in which I assume priors are set on unstandardized coefficients)?</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "CPxH8RNBAAAJ",
   "from": "Paul Buerkner",
   "author": "6e3dd74b422c061b",
   "date": "2018-04-04T21:17:20Z",
   "subject": "Re: [brms-users] Coefficient estimates are unstandardized?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>The scale of the coefficients depends on the scale of the variables\r\n(i.e. they are unstandardized) as is the case for most other ordinary regression functions.<br><br></div>Thus, If you want your coefficients to be standarized, you have to standardize your variables.<br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">2018-04-04 23:01 GMT+02:00 David Sidhu <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">dms...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span>:<br></div></div>"
